# Project: Site Operations Dashboard

Full-stack app for managing sites, installations, and operational summaries.
Built for a technical evaluation — prioritize clean, working code over extra features.

## Stack
- Frontend: React.js (Vite), React Hooks, axios/fetch for REST calls
- Backend: Node.js + Express
- Database: PostgreSQL (local for dev, Azure Database for PostgreSQL for deploy)
- Deployment: Azure App Service (backend) + Azure Static Web Apps (frontend)

## Progress Tracking
Read `PROJECT_CHECKLIST.md` at the start of every session. Resume from the
first unchecked `- [ ]` task. Mark tasks `- [x]` only after the code is
written AND verified working (server starts, endpoint returns expected
response, UI renders without errors) — not just written.

## Database Schema
```sql
Sites (id, name, location, status, created_at)
Installations (id, site_id -> Sites.id, equipment_type, status, notes)
```
- Installations.site_id is NOT NULL, ON DELETE CASCADE

## Conventions
- REST routes: `/api/sites`, `/api/sites/:id`, `/api/installations`,
  `/api/installations/:id`, `/api/summary`
- Error responses: `{ "error": "message" }` with appropriate 4xx/5xx status
- Use `express-validator` for input validation on POST/PUT routes
- Use a connection pool (`pg.Pool`), never a single client
- Env vars only for config/secrets — never hardcode DB credentials
- Folder structure: `/server` (Express API), `/client` (React app)
- Commits: small and incremental, one logical change per commit — no giant
  end-of-day commits
